From 11ca7029a1536aed91face314aed6abafce4a46c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: orchestration-renewed <agent@creation-guidelines>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 13:29:53 +0100
Subject: [RFC PATCH 1/4] dt-bindings: watchdog: qcom,pm8916-wdt: Add PM8998
 and wakeup-source

The PMIC watchdog of the PON block is also present in the second
generation PON found in PM8998 and later PMICs (PM6150, PM8150...), at
the same offsets in the PON_HLOS peripheral; only the power-off reason
registers moved. Add a compatible for it.

Allow wakeup-source: the bark interrupt is a PMIC interrupt that can wake
the system, like the power key's, which lets the watchdog keep counting
through system suspend when wakeup is enabled for it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/watchdog/qcom,pm8916-wdt.yaml  | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/watchdog/qcom,pm8916-wdt.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/watchdog/qcom,pm8916-wdt.yaml
index a519422c3..004992cb1 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/watchdog/qcom,pm8916-wdt.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/watchdog/qcom,pm8916-wdt.yaml
@@ -14,10 +14,18 @@ allOf:
 
 properties:
   compatible:
-    const: qcom,pm8916-wdt
+    enum:
+      - qcom,pm8916-wdt
+      - qcom,pm8998-wdt
 
   interrupts:
     maxItems: 1
+    description: Bark (pre-timeout) interrupt of the watchdog.
+
+  wakeup-source:
+    description:
+      The bark may wake the system, which lets the watchdog keep counting
+      through system suspend when wakeup is enabled for it.
 
 required:
   - compatible
-- 
